I think this is the right time to stop thinking of the application as "an AI trading app" and start thinking of it as an **AI Quant Operating System (AIQOS)**. The four workspaces shouldn't be separate applications—they should share the same data, strategies, portfolio state, AI agents, and execution engine. A strategy should move seamlessly from research to backtesting, then to paper trading, and finally to live trading without being rewritten.

Here's the architecture I'd recommend.

# AI Quant Operating System (AIQOS)

```
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|                     AI QUANT OPERATING SYSTEM                 |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

            Research Workspace
                    │
                    ▼
           Backtesting Workspace
                    │
                    ▼
          Paper Trading Workspace
                    │
                    ▼
           Live Trading Workspace

---------------------------------------------------------------

Shared Services

AI Agents
Feature Engine
Data Lake
Strategy Registry
Portfolio Engine
Risk Engine
Broker Layer
Experiment Tracking
Notification Service
Authentication
```

Every workspace uses the same underlying services.

